         "colour": "#8a6138",
         "_comment_height_2026_08_31": "Was 2.00m (D19). BACKLOG-VISUAL-STARTER-SCALE/BACKLOG-VISUAL-BADGER-LINE-SCALE (see `_comment_starter_scale_2026_08_31` above): 2.00m rendered taller than the 1.80m trainer AND taller than this line's own adult, Burrowback (1.70m, untouched by this pass) -- a starter should not loom over the player, and a cub should not outsize the adult it is thematically paired with in the census. Dropped to 1.62m, verified by direct re-render (creature_body._fit() at this height is comfortably below its footprint-volume clamp threshold for this model, so the render-measured height equals the declared 1.62m exactly -- checked, not assumed). `radius` dropped by the identical ratio (0.81x) per D12's 'radii scale with height' rule, so the hit cone and catch-accuracy bonus stay tuned relative to the creature's own new size rather than becoming proportionally larger. SUPERSEDED 2026-09-01, see `_comment_height_2026_09_01_correction` below -- kept verbatim as the historical record of what the 08-31 pass did and why, not amended.",
         "_comment_height_2026_09_01_correction": "OD-0901-1 (`archive/owner/OWNER_DIRECTIVES_2026-09-01.md`): the owner directly overrode the 08-31 cut above -- 'I think almost all creatures should stand taller than the character. That's part of the allure of the game.' A starter looming over the player is the intended read, not the defect the census called it. Raised to 2.30m: past the pre-08-31 value of 2.00m (D19), not merely back to it, per the owner's explicit instruction not to just undo the cut. `radius` raised by the same ratio in reverse (radius/height held at Terrapup's own 0.3802 constant, per D12), giving 0.8746 -- so the hit cone and catch-accuracy bonus track the new size exactly as they tracked the old one. Verified by direct re-render with tools/_capture_creature_roster.gd: render-measured height equals the declared 2.30m (creature_body._fit()'s footprint-volume clamp does not engage at this height for this model). Burrowback (the 'badger line' pairing from defect 65) is deliberately left untouched -- see the ripplet entry's 2026-09-01 comment for the reasoning, which applies equally here.",
+        "_comment_species_dog3_1024": "Coordinator Meshy terrapup_dog3 c1 (tb/meshy-1024 42c192cbb: Bernese/Saint-Bernard redraft after GPU 7.09 read dog2 as an otter; provenance assets_raw/naturalistic-1024/terrapup_dog3/provenance.jsonl). Raw L/H 1.53 (dog2 1.66). Measured quadruped rig at 3.20 m (4.90 m long), dog2 clips with the +90 side-lying faint. Seat 2.58 m at z 0.0: lower and forward of dog2 (2.66 at -0.21), just under the back top (2.63-2.70 m there).",
+        "_comment_species_dog2_1024": "Owner 24 Oct: \"Terrapup is supposed to be a large dog, not a badger.\" Coordinator Meshy terrapup_dog2 c2 (mountain dog, brown coat, cream blaze/chest, teal eyes, mossy stone plates, amber seams; provenance candidate_dog2/source/meshy_provenance.jsonl), measured quadruped rig at 3.20 m, the nat1022 pilot clips. close-1024 b21 CPU sanity 7.46 vs the badger 7.65 (badger ruled wrong species); GPU to decide.",
         "height": 3.2,
