         "_comment_rest_roll": "OWNER-0912-TERRAPUP-LAY R41 keeps whole-body runtime roll disabled. The installed GLB now carries a dedicated authored rest clip: its skeletal root rolls around the rig's verified flank axis while the four legs, head, spine and tail fold as one animation. This replaces the R25-R38 attempt to rescue the crouching faint clip with runtime transforms.",
         "rest_roll_deg": 0.0,
-        "field_rim": 0.25,
+        "field_rim": 0.3,
         "rest_use_body_pose": true,
         "_comment_rest_pose": "R41 uses the dedicated baked rest clip and applies only a measured model translation after the clip completes. The final 90-degree flank pose uses mirrored local-Z limb tucks. The live-skin probe excludes CreatureBody's four-vertex ContactShadow helper from anatomical bounds: R40 grounded that helper while the visible creature hovered. The real unshifted skinned minimum is 1.1302m below the anchor plane, so +1.0302m targets 0.100m of bedding compression. The no-op root recipe preserves the authored final frame through the reversible rest lifecycle; no runtime skeletal distortion, mesh scaling or vertex deformation is used.",
         "_comment_rest_nat1022": "Close-1024: the naturalistic pilot's own rest clip ends grounded (author_native_clips.py grounds every frame; Blender: lowest vertex 0.00 m, 3.05 m tall = 0.79 of standing), so the installed model's +1.0302 m translation is 0.",
