         "_comment_field_emission_0901": "OWNER DIRECTIVE 2026-09-01 ('some of the smaller creatures blend into the environment too well'), revisited 2026-09-25 under the owner's lane-session direction that Terrapup's shell is grey STONE (sheet 01) and should 'look good'. History: 1.4 was chosen on 09-01 when the shell was an olive/mint block, from a sweep that put 1.4 at 1.124/1.070 on that texture and that probe framing. Re-measured 2026-09-25 on the stone-plate texture with tools/_probe_grass_separation.gd --species=terrapup --extra-emission=0.6,0.8,1.0,1.2,1.4 and tools/_grass_separation_ratio.py, creature box (490,225)-(795,445) vs grass boxes (150,260,380,340) / (100,440,420,640): DAY 0.6->0.635/0.762, 0.8->0.685/0.822, 1.0->0.725/0.870, 1.2->0.753/0.907, 1.4->0.776/0.935; NIGHT 0.6->0.444/0.531, 1.0->0.510/0.611, 1.4->0.574/0.688. No value up to 1.4 reaches the old 1.06 luminance target in the current probe framing (the box is mostly shaded coat), so 1.4 no longer meets it either; the trend would need ~3.0, which renders the plates white and the moss lime (seen in the 2026-09-25 world A/B). 0.6 is kept because separation now comes from the pale grey plates against the dark coat and the green field (hue and in-body value contrast), which two code-blind judge rounds preferred to the 1.4 look ('grey-on-brown contrast lifts the silhouette day and night'). The 1.06 luminance bar is therefore NOT claimed as met at 0.6. TUNABLE.",
